From 7b171f6969bea9f8a1d99b61b7be5c0bf931722c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:29:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Validation gate and routing: validate.py, route.py

validate.py checks a model against its TO on one voxel grid: one solid, volume
within 10 %, overlap at least 70 % both ways, largest missed and extra regions
at most 5 % of the TO, stand-in agreement. swtruss.py runs it at the end, and
its SolidWorks script ends with a validation line (sketches fully defined,
links made, features and final volume as built).

route.py picks plates, heightfield, truss, frame (candidate) or none from
analysis.json and a planar-truss test (axis-aligned domain filling its box,
mirror plane, medial material on the box face planes). Case 7 routes to truss;
route.json and validation.json written for the case studies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BdLZZ8R4FqXDzDRWDvVnZQ
